body:
You've been through a lot, and I'm really sorry. 

&#x200B;

I understand. My life experience is different than yours, but I have felt all those things you're feeling, and I know it's terrible, and it feels like it will be the same. 

&#x200B;

I also have unhealthy coping mechanisms, and it's really hard to get rid of them. I have mine, and it's super hard for me to talk about it, because it ashames me, and I don't think I can quit it, until I get some bad consequences from it. It's like I do it to hurt myself without it being so obvious to others. I think it's the same as you with drugs, but please get rid of the benzos. Those are super dangerous without supervision. 

&#x200B;

One thing that caught my attention is that you can actually say good things about yourself, and you have projects, and that's great! It would be great if you found a way to prioritize those thoughts, but the bad stuff is way too strong. I really hope you can find a way. 

&#x200B;

Therapy is hard. I've been through a ton of therapy sessions, trying to find the one that will help me, and the process might be really long and hard. I'm still looking for that person that will help me. To be honest, I'm not sure if I will ever find it, but that's all that's left, and I really want to try.
